{"type":"message","id":"f15c089f","parentId":"c4aa9943","timestamp":"2026-03-31T05:57:57.220Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Actually, using raw WebSocket with PowerShell is complex. Let me try a simpler approach - use Chrome's `--app` mode with a JavaScript bookmarklet or just type the values using UI Automation.\n\nActually, the simplest approach would be to use PowerShell's UI Automation to find the Chrome window and simulate typing into the input fields.\n\nLet me try a different, simpler approach:\n1. Use Chrome remote debugging with a simpler HTTP-based approach\n2. Or use Selenium-like automation\n\nActually, the simplest approach is to use Chrome's `chrome://settings/` or just use PowerShell to inject JavaScript via a temporary bookmarklet. But with CDP over HTTP/WebSocket, it's a bit complex.\n\n\nI think UI Automation through PowerShell would be the most straightforward path here.","thinkingSignature":"50ff9d6773dd70677dd656de79bf9230be813bdf2b83c3b17f49557b08299f64"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_f3f9l2g6amdh_1","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.openclaw\\workspace\\uia_fill.ps1","content":"Add-Type -AssemblyName UIAutomationClient\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName UIAutomationTypes\n\n$username = \"18926879306\"\n$password = \"100911yzpYZP\"\n\n# Find Chrome window\n$chromeProcs = Get-Process -Name chrome -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.MainWindowHandle -ne 0 }\nif (-not $chromeProcs) {\n    Write-Host \"No Chrome window found\"\n    exit 1\n}\nWrite-Host \"Found Chrome window with handle: $($chromeProcs[0].MainWindowHandle)\"\n\n$chromeHandle = $chromeProcs[0].MainWindowHandle\n$condition = New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ProcessIdProperty, $chromeProcs[0].Id)\n$root = [System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::FromHandle($chromeHandle)\n\n# Find all document/edit fields\n$editCondition = New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ControlTypeProperty, [System.Windows.Automation.ControlType]::Edit)\n$textBoxCondition = New-Object System.Windows.Automation.OrCondition(\n    (New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ControlTypeProperty, [System.Windows.Automation.ControlType]::Edit)),\n    (New-Object System.Windows.Automation.PropertyCondition([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationElement]::ControlTypeProperty, [System.Windows.Automation.ControlType]::Document))\n)\n\n$elements = $root.FindAll([System.Windows.Automation.TreeScope]::Descendants, $textBoxCondition)\nWrite-Host \"Found $($elements.Count) text elements\"\n\n$foundCount = 0\nforeach ($el in $elements) {\n    $name = $el.Current.Name\n    $className = $el.Current.ClassName\n    $isEnabled = $el.Current.IsEnabled\n    $rect = $el.Current.BoundingRectangle\n    \n    Write-Host \"  Element: Name='$name' Class='$className' Enabled=$isEnabled Rect=$rect\"\n    \n    if ($isEnabled -and $rect.Width -gt 50 -and $rect.Height -gt 10) {\n        try {\n            $valuePattern = $el.GetCurrentPattern([System.Windows.Automation.AutomationPattern]::LookupById([System.Windows.Automation.ValuePattern]::Pattern))\n            if ($valuePattern) {\n                if ($foundCount -eq 0) {\n                    $valuePattern.SetValue($username)\n                    Write-Host \"  -> Filled username: $username\"\n                    $foundCount++\n                } elseif ($foundCount -eq 1) {\n                    $valuePattern.SetValue($password)\n                    Write-Host \"  -> Filled password: [hidden]\"\n                    $foundCount++\n                }\n            }\n        } catch {\n            Write-Host \"  -> Could not set value: $_\"\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nif ($foundCount -eq 0) {\n    Write-Host \"No editable fields found, trying direct SendKeys...\"\n    # Fallback: use SendKeys\n    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500\n    [System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait($username)\n    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200\n    [System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait(\"{TAB}\")\n    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200\n    [System.Windows.Forms.SendKeys]::SendWait($password)\n    Write-Host \"Sent via SendKeys\"\n} else {\n    Write-Host \"Successfully filled $foundCount fields via UIA\"\n}\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":3531,"output":931,"cacheRead":19925,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24387,"cost":{"input":0.0010593,"output":0.0011172,"cacheRead":0.0011955,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003372}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774936651241,"responseId":"061a954b4ac49bc0e9897bf1564cd3c0"}}
